## Problem Understanding

A **shadow pair** (i, j) must satisfy:
1. 0 ≤ i < j < n
2. nums[i] < nums[j]
3. There is NO index k where i < k < j and nums[i] < nums[k] < nums[j]

In other words, for a valid shadow pair (i, j), there should be no element strictly between nums[i] and nums[j] in the subarray from index i+1 to j-1.

## Key Insight

For a pair (i, j) to be a shadow pair, there should be no element in the range (i, j) that lies in the open interval (nums[i], nums[j]).

This means that nums[j] is the first element after index i that is greater than nums[i], but also that there's no element between nums[i] and nums[j] in between.

